  "metric_definitions": {
    "z-euclid": "per-coordinate z-score over the reference symbol set, unweighted Euclidean, then rescaled so the mean off-diagonal distance is 1 (unit_scale)",
    "z-whiten": "z-euclid then full PCA whitening over the same reference set, same rescaling",
    "old-fitted": "metric16.json weights; OLD ONLY, Gate 1 only, reported as circular"
  },
  "comparability_cost": "z-scoring reads the spread of each coordinate off the evaluation symbols. Closed inside Gate 3 (train-fold statistics only); NOT closed inside Gate 1, identically for both bases, so only the old-vs-new difference there is meaningful. Whitening strips each basis of its own correlation structure, which would otherwise decide the answer, because the new tongue coords are near-collinear. The unit_scale rescaling is a further assumption: it assumes a confusable pair sits at a fixed FRACTION of the mean consonant-consonant distance in either basis, which is not something either basis guarantees.",
